<title>UK: UK's Halma buys alarm siren firm Klaxon.</title>
<headline>UK's Halma buys alarm siren firm Klaxon.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British security systems maker Halma Plc said on Thursday it had bought alarm siren company Klaxon Signals Ltd for about 1.27 million stg.</p>
<p>Halma said it would also provide funds to enable Klaxon to repay 359,000 stg of loan notes due to vendors.</p>
<p>Klaxon had a pretax profit, after adding back non-recurring costs, of 227,000 stg on turnover of 2.21 million stg for the year ended April 30.</p>
<p>Halma's shares were flat at 195.5p at 0956 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
